contributors, and are released under the same licence (AGPL-3.0-only).
The full upstream history is kept in this repository's git history.

This notice is given under section 5(a) of the AGPL: the work has been
modified, and the changes below are dated relative to the base above.

Modifications (2026-11-13 onwards)
----------------------------------

- Added "Learn anything": a roadmap builder. You type what you want to
  learn and pick a depth (Normal, High, Super, Ultra, Ultraviolet). Up to
  three quick questions settle your starting level, then a staged roadmap
  streams in with topics, prerequisites and resources per stage.
  New code lives in src/core/learn/, src/agent/learn/, src/store/learn.ts,
  src/server/learn*.ts, app/learn/, app/api/learn/ and components/learn/.
- Added source adapters for Wikipedia, MIT Learn/OCW, freeCodeCamp, Open
  Library, official documentation (robots.txt respected), the YouTube
  Data API v3 (your own key), arXiv, Semantic Scholar, Hacker News
  (Algolia), GitHub awesome-lists and, optionally, Brave Search.
- Added a timeline view and a star-map view for roadmaps, per-topic
  progress, and a postMessage/HTTP bridge that hands Flashcards and
  Calendar payloads to rika (docs/learn.md).
- Added a daily spending limit for roadmap model calls, with a review
  sheet when a build would go over it.
- Added the "roadmap" background model role (defaults to the cheap
  model slot) to the existing provider layer, a YouTube key entry to the
  key list, a "Learn" settings section and a "Learn" entry in the sidebar.
- Added rika module packaging: rika-module.json, scripts/package-module
  and .github/workflows/module-release.yml.
- The upstream desktop release workflow (.github/workflows/release.yml)
  no longer runs on tag pushes; it can still be run by hand. Tags in this
  fork publish the rika module instead.
- The package version is 0.4.0-rika.1. The npm package name stays
  "learnharness" so desktop data folders and provider attribution do not move.

All other LearnHarness features are kept as they are.
